Welcome to this changelog !

=================================================================

1.0.0 - November 20th 2026 : First stable release (PowerShell)

 - The PowerShell script is now the main version ; the batch script
   (0.6.0-beta) is marked as RETIRED and kept for reference only
 - New console UI : framed headers, colored menus and keys, step indicator,
   confirmation screen with sizes, codec, free space and warnings
 - Live progress dashboard while DISM runs : name of the current edition,
   per-edition and overall progress bar (weighted by edition size),
   remaining time of the current edition, elapsed time, throughput,
   bytes written, free disk space, DISM memory (current / peak),
   CPU usage, system RAM usage,
   list of completed editions
 - Progress in the window title and in the Windows Terminal tab / taskbar
 - Final statistics : size before / after, difference, ratio, codec of
   source and destination (read from the WIM header), duration, throughput, peak memory, CPU time, per-edition table,
   verification of the destination, FAT32 (4 GB) hint
 - Save the statistics as a text report ('R' key or -ReportPath parameter)
 - Export several editions at once (e.g. 1,3-5), also via -Index
 - Hints for common DISM error codes (disk full, access denied, ...)
 - Fallback progress (Write-Progress / text lines) for PowerShell ISE and
   redirected output

=================================================================

0.7.0-beta - November 18th 2026 : PowerShell edition

 - New PowerShell script Simple-WIM2ESD---ESD2WIM-Converter.ps1 with the
   same interactive menus as the batch script
 - Non-interactive mode via parameters (-Mode, -Source, -Destination,
   -Compression, -Index) with exit codes for automation
 - Index list read with a single DISM call, now also shows index sizes
 - Refuse identical source and destination paths (prevents deleting the
   source image)
 - Create a missing destination folder automatically
 - Show the DISM output on the error screen when reading the image fails
 - The batch script is still included and unchanged

=================================================================

0.6.0-beta - August 8th 2026 : Bugfix release (fork)

 - Use the DISM installed with the OS by default (always up to date) ;
   the bundled DISM folder is only used as a fallback
 - Fix empty index names in the index list (FOR variable collision)
 - Fix support for paths containing spaces (proper quoting everywhere,
   user-pasted quotes are stripped automatically)
 - Fix crash caused by GOTO to the non-existent label "IndexExport"
 - Fix the broken Administrator elevation prompt (invalid SET params syntax)
 - Fix the start-over flow ('S') which re-ran parts of the script twice
 - Fix error detection : DISM exit codes are now actually checked,
   including inside the "export all indexes" loop
 - Fix index parsing on non-English systems (DISM is called with /English)
 - ESD -> WIM preset now uses Maximum compression instead of Recovery
 - Add input validation for the index number and an existence check
   for the source image
 - Add a clear error screen when no DISM executable can be found

=================================================================

0.5.0-beta - April 1st 2018 : Initial Creation

